THREAD POOL : A Thread Pool is a collection of pre-created and reusable worker threads that execute multiple tasks.
              Instead of creating a new thread for every task, the same threads are reused to execute different tasks.

Advantages of Thread Pool
             ~  Thread Reusability
             ~  Reduces Thread Creation Overhead
             ~  Better Resource Management
             ~  Improves Performance
             ~  Task Management : Tasks can be submitted to the pool and are executed by available worker threads.
             ~  Controls Concurrency : We can control how many tasks execute simultaneously by controlling the number of worker threads.

Executors Framework in Java : The Executors framework was introduced in Java 5 as part of the java.util.concurrent
              package to simplify the development of concurrent applications by abstracting away many of the complexities involved in creating and managing threads.

Problem which was coming Prior to Executors Framework
             ~  Manual Thread Management
             ~  Resource Management is tough
             ~  Scalability
             ~  Thread Reuse
             ~  Error Handling

